# Third-party components

contexture-runtime, the image published from this repository, redistributes no harness. Hermes
Agent, the Hermes Web UI, Claude Code, Codex, agy, ctxr, cb and agent-browser are each downloaded
from their publishers by the store that runs the image, at its first boot, into that store's own
volume. Their licences are their publishers' terms with that store, not part of this image.

What the image does install at build time, as published binaries or packages:

  Debian packages (debian:trixie-slim and apt)   per-package licences in /usr/share/doc/*/copyright
  Node.js          https://nodejs.org                       MIT and others (LICENSE in the tarball)
  gh (GitHub CLI)  https://github.com/cli/cli               MIT
  restic           https://github.com/restic/restic         BSD-2-Clause
  rclone           https://github.com/rclone/rclone         MIT
  pandoc           https://github.com/jgm/pandoc            GPL-2.0-or-later
  jq               https://github.com/jqlang/jq             MIT
  Python packages in /opt/contexture/venv (pypdf, reportlab, pdfplumber, pypdfium2, python-docx,
  openpyxl, python-pptx, beautifulsoup4)                    their own licences, in the venv's metadata

Earlier releases also published contexture-hermes, built on nousresearch/hermes-agent with the
Hermes Web UI grafted in (both MIT); its NOTICE is in this repository's history.
